    "text": "A coil having inductance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> and resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is connected to a battery of emf <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ε</mi></math>&nbsp;at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are the times for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>%</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>99</mn><mo>%</mo></math> completion of the current growth in the circuit, then&nbsp;<math>&nbsp;<mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mtext>t</mtext> <mn>1</mn> </msub> </mrow> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>t</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;will be",
